{"ts":1793396674140,"event":"done","summary":"PLAT-103: validateApp now throws when app.owner is missing or empty (shared-contracts bumped to 2.0.0, breaking). core-shell (platform) and sub-route-billing (payments) pass owner from their package.json team. Also fixed sub-route-reports (insights), which was not in the ticket but calls validateApp and would otherwise throw. Three PRs (#1 contract+reports, #2 billing, #3 shell), merged in dependency order; CI and CD green on each; st audit reports 0 violations. Assumptions: 'empty' means falsy (no whitespace trimming); owner values are hardcoded to match package.json because bundles cannot read package.json at runtime; shared-contracts is inlined at build time, so 'release' is the merge plus the major version bump, with no registry publish."}
